A||||18||fiero56||what should I do||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||07-06-2000||09:59 PM||||Well, I have been in contact with Ed lately about labor on installing poly bushings for me. He says to expect $250-$350 labor plus the cost of alignment($100, he doesn't have the machine, he sends the cars out to another guy to do that). So expecting everything goes well, thats $350 labor and alignment. Then I have to add the cost of around $150 for the bushings, that makes it $500, not to mention the cost of driving down there, hotel one night, driving back, food, gas, etc, =too much. <BR>What should I do? If I take it to Ed, I know the work will be done right. But it will cost me some $$$. If I do it local(I haven't shopped around here yet), I'm not guaranteed everything will be perfect(putting the car on a lift incorrectly is enough to scare me away). But, it might be cheaper(read that, more affordable).<P>Don't get me wrong, I think $250 to install poly bushings at all 4 corners is excellent. Probably the best price I will find. But that $100 alignment and everything else added, just takes the price higher than I would like, with nationals and everything coming up.<P>Can anyone recommend a good shop to do the work? I haven't been able to think of any, and I don't know anyone who has had suspension work done. The only few places I used for my last car(mercury sable= VERY easy car to work on)they fu**** it up everytime I took it in(I had to take it home and fix <B>their</B> mistakes). Never going there again.<P>Any good shops to recommend suspension work?||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||07-06-2000||10:04 PM||||I don't have an answer for you but there are enough Fieros in the Southern Ohio (where exactly <I>are</I> you anyway??) and Central KY area that we oughtta find a good shop -- I just got back here for a while from CA where the Fiero Shop did all the work on mine -- maybe we could talk George into flying out here for a couple of days............nahhh....anyway, I'll look around down here (Lexington) and in northern KY when I go up there tomorrow and see what I can find.........<P>------------------<BR>My '87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero/</A><BR> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
