Z||000003||Oreif||07-06-2000||10:49 PM||||How about Bob Steiger at Twin Lakes Fiero? He's right here in ILL. Give him a call at 217-379-9140<BR>He's only 261 miles from Dayton! (5 hour drive). You could probably leave early from your house, get to his place around 9-10am and he could most likely get you back on the road by early evening. No Hotel/Motel to pay and depending on gas mileage 2-3 tanks of gas.<P>------------------<BR>~Oreif~<BR>Fieroholic and proud of it!<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||07-06-2000||10:57 PM||||thanks fiero56, no need to be precise, I was just trying to get a feel for the area......Southern OH could have been somewhere like, Portsmouth...........anyway, there seems to be quite a few Fiero owners on the I-75 corridor -- <P>Oreif, that's not a bad idea -- there just aren't many in this country who really know and specialize in the Fiero -- mine sure isn't going to the local Pontiac dealer!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||07-06-2000||11:36 PM||||I'll give him a call tommorrow morning. He is actually a little closer to me than Ed Parkss, but Ed has TONS of neat stuff out back to check out <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||07-06-2000||11:44 PM||||Bob has over 96 Fiero's laying around. Not to mention the 3.4L, 3800, and V-8 swaps that are "work in progress" to check-out.<BR>He even has usually 6-10 cars for sale. You could take a test drive to get lunch in one!<BR>Also it would be a good time to mill around his many parts shelves for any parts you may need. He has 4 large rooms filled (and organized) with many parts. ||||reg||1
